# Shell scripts and Gradle wrappers MUST stay LF on checkout, on every platform.
# A CR in a shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r", and
# the failure is opaque: "cannot execute: required file not found" for a file
# that is plainly there. This already cost a debugging round on ./gradlew in this
# repo, and deploy/demo/entrypoint.sh would fail the same way inside a container
# where there is nothing to debug with.
*.sh        text eol=lf
gradlew     text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
